[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2296523331","pull_request_review_id":3149186187,"id":2296523331,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6I4ipD","diff_hunk":"@@ -79,8 +79,11 @@ Vector<String> ResourceLoader::get_recognized_extensions_for_type(const String &\n \tList<String> exts;\n \t::ResourceLoader::get_recognized_extensions_for_type(p_type, &exts);\n \tVector<String> ret;\n+\tret.resize(exts.size());\n+\tint idx = 0;\n+\n \tfor (const String &E : exts) {\n-\t\tret.push_back(E);\n+\t\tret.set(idx++, E);","path":"core/core_bind.cpp","commit_id":"b356bc1a36b321dc4e604bcbd55a2357ba411fdd","original_commit_id":"b356bc1a36b321dc4e604bcbd55a2357ba411fdd","user":{"login":"YYF233333","id":67693830,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NjkzODMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67693830?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333","html_url":"https://github.com/YYF233333","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Just a reminder: the `Vector` type has a `ptrw` method that allows us to avoid performing boundary checks and COW (Copy-On-Write) on every write operation. However, this makes the code a bit more complex since you need to obtain the write pointer outside the loop first.\r\n\r\nAs for this particular case, I believe the final solution should be to have `: